{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>יחילו</b> — Rabbi Moses the Kohen said: the meaning of 'his ways' is his desires, like 'a man's heart devises his way' (Proverbs 16:9), and the meaning of יחילו is 'they shall come,' like 'they shall come upon the head of Joab' (1 Kings 2:32), and the sense is that his needs come to him and are prepared for him according to his desire. Or: 'the ways of Elohim' is the meaning, and the sense of יחילו is that it would have been fitting to terrify him, from the root חיל. But the correct view in my eyes: יחילו is a verb from the root חיל, like יולדה, and the pu'al is defective, like לא תרצח." "<b>ודרכיו</b> — It returns to the wicked: his ways terrify the discerning, because they succeed." "<b>מרום</b> — like 'You are on high forever, O YHWH' (Psalms 92:9); it is a noun. The meaning: 'You are on high' — Your judgments are removed from before him." "<b>וטעם יפיח בהם</b> — like 'scoffers inflame a city' (Proverbs 29:8)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra proposes that יחילו is a defective form of יחוֹלַל (pu'al), hence comparing it to לא תרצח where a quiescent vav drops; יולדה cited as parallel root pattern.", 2 "Resolved 'והוא השם' as 'it is a noun' (i.e., מרום functions as a substantive); could also read 'and it is the Name,' but context favors noun."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:56.432634700Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}